WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.453 --> 00:00:01.995
- [Narrator] This is Gemma.

00:00:01.995 --> 00:00:05.298
Nearly eight feet tall, she
is one big Bactrian camel,

00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:08.631
the largest of all living camel species.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:16.464
Gemma is 15 years old, which
places her at middle age

00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:18.133
for Bactrian camels.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.955
Native to the steppes of Central Asia,

00:00:20.955 --> 00:00:23.112
Bactrian camels have two humps, not one.

00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:25.560
And contrary to what many people think,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.003
their humps contain fat, not water.

00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:30.542
They convert the stored fat into energy,

00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:33.043
which can be used in
place of water or food.

00:00:33.043 --> 00:00:35.979
This, along with their clumpy, wooly coats

00:00:35.979 --> 00:00:38.354
and tolerance for high
altitudes, make them the perfect

00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:41.365
companions for long, difficult journeys.

00:00:41.365 --> 00:00:44.184
Domesticated Bactrian camels are abundant,

00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:46.323
but wild ones are critically endangered

00:00:46.323 --> 00:00:48.885
due to hunting and loss of habitat.

00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:50.654
Over the course of the next couple

00:00:50.654 --> 00:00:53.182
of generations, their numbers
outside of domesticity

00:00:53.182 --> 00:00:55.432
are expected to dwindle to just a quarter

00:00:55.432 --> 00:00:58.263
of its current population.

00:00:58.263 --> 00:01:00.513
This is the Bactrian camel.

00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:06.884
(digital tone)

